---
description: Builder.io Gen-2 SDK usage rules.
globs: app/**/*.{ts,tsx}, components/builder/**, builder-registry.ts, config.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

- Use `RenderBuilderContent`, never `<Content>` directly.
- Reference models via `config.models.*`, never as string literals.
- `notFound()` when `fetchOneEntry` returns null on a Builder-only route.
- `getBuilderSearchParams` only inside `app/preview/page.tsx`.
- Preview renders pass `disableTracking` to `RenderBuilderContent` (requires `@builder.io/sdk-react@5.2.4+`) so the Builder A/B initializer cannot leak as visible React 19 content. Never pass `isNestedRender` on the root content being edited in `app/preview/page.tsx` — it is internal-only and disables the visual editor's drag/drop `postMessage` listener.
- In `app/preview/page.tsx`, never render sibling components next to the `RenderBuilderContent` instance being edited (mirror the sibling-free `<RenderBuilderContent />` return in `app/[...page]/page.tsx`) — siblings can trigger a live-editing DOM reconciliation bug that leaks the SDK's personalization-init script as visible text.
- HTML fields → `utils/sanitize-html.ts`.
- Re-export Builder field types from `types/*.types.ts` with `string | null`.
